        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Raju saw the great Brihadisvara temple at Thanjavur.\n\"Rajaraja Chola built it,\" said the guide."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "Chola",
          "navy",
          "sultanate"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The Cholas of the south, under Rajaraja I and Rajendra I, built a strong empire with a navy that reached South-East Asia. They built the Brihadisvara temple and had an organised village administration.\nIn the north Mahmud of Ghazni raided India and later Muhammad Ghori defeated Prithviraj Chauhan at the second Battle of Tarain in 1192.\nThe Delhi Sultanate began in 1206 with Qutb-ud-din Aibak."
        }
